{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++11 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++11 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\ntypedef long long ll;\n\nset<ll> visited;\n\nbool wasVisited(ll c) {\n    return visited.find(c) != visited.end();\n}\n\nvoid generateSteps(ll n, vector<step>& out) {\n    // compute all repunits up to n+1\n    vector<ll> reps;\n    ll r = 0;\n    while (r <= n + 1) {\n        r = r * 10 + 1;\n        reps.push_back(r);\n    }\n    // lower\n    ll low = 0;\n    int lowCost = 0;\n    for (int i = 0; i < (int)reps.size(); ++i) {\n        if (reps[i] <= n) {\n            low = reps[i];\n            lowCost = i + 1;\n        }\n    }\n    ll res = low;\n    int cost = lowCost;\n    while (res + low <= n) {\n        res += low;\n        cost += lowCost;\n    }\n    out.push_back({res, cost});\n    // upper\n    res = low;\n    cost = lowCost;\n    while (res < n) {\n        res += low;\n        cost += lowCost;\n    }\n    out.push_back({res, cost});\n    // uupper\n    ll uu = 0;\n    int uuCost = 0;\n    for (int i = 0; i < (int)reps.size(); ++i) {\n        if (reps[i] >= n) {\n            uu = reps[i];\n            uuCost = i + 1;\n            break;\n        }\n    }\n    out.push_back({uu, uuCost});\n}\n\nint main(int argc, char **argv) {\n    ll n;\n    cin >> n;\n    priority_queue<step> pq;\n    pq.push({n, 0});\n    while (pq.top().val != 0) {\n        ll val = pq.top().val;\n        int cost = pq.top().cost;\n        pq.pop();\n        if (wasVisited(val))\n            continue;\n        visited.insert(val);\n        vector<step> steps;\n        generateSteps(val, steps);\n        for (step next : steps) {\n            next.cost += cost;\n            next.val = abs(val - next.val);\n            pq.push(next);\n        }\n    }\n    cout << pq.top().cost << endl;\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\nimport heapq\n\nvisited = set()\n\ndef was_visited(c):\n    return c in visited\n\ndef generate_steps(n, out):\n    # compute all repunits up to n+1\n    reps = []\n    r = 0\n    while r <= n + 1:\n        r = r * 10 + 1\n        reps.append(r)\n    # lower\n    low = 0\n    low_cost = 0\n    for i, rep in enumerate(reps):\n        if rep <= n:\n            low = rep\n            low_cost = i + 1\n    res = low\n    cost = low_cost\n    while res + low <= n:\n        res += low\n        cost += low_cost\n    out.append([res, cost])\n    # upper\n    res = low\n    cost = low_cost\n    while res < n:\n        res += low\n        cost += low_cost\n    out.append([res, cost])\n    # uupper\n    uu = 0\n    uu_cost = 0\n    for i, rep in enumerate(reps):\n        if rep >= n:\n            uu = rep\n            uu_cost = i + 1\n            break\n    out.append([uu, uu_cost])\n\ndef main():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().strip().split()\n    if not data:\n        return\n    n = int(data[0])\n    pq = []\n    heapq.heappush(pq, [n, 0])\n    while pq[0][0] != 0:\n        val, cost = heapq.heappop(pq)\n        if was_visited(val):\n            continue\